# ByteSizeICT — Cursor Agent Rules
# Canonical, more detailed version: CLAUDE.md (keep both in sync; CLAUDE.md wins on conflict).

## Pre-flight (every task)
Before any edit or mutating command, read IN FULL, in order:
1. docs/01_PRD.md      (scope, user stories, NON-GOALS)
2. docs/02_AppFlow.md  (routes, guards, state machines, screens, error codes)
3. docs/03_UI_Spec.md  (design tokens, component states)
4. docs/04_TRD.md      (locked stack + exact versions, folder structure, API contracts, security)
5. docs/05_Schema.md   (DDL, RLS, SQL functions, auth flow)
6. docs/06_Plan.md     (V1 checklist + Decision Log: history/context)
7. docs/07_Plan_V2.md  (ACTIVE checklist for R1.1/V2; find "Current Step", owner decisions §2, free-tier rules §3)
Then state which plan step you are executing. If the request maps to no step, ask before proceeding.
docs 01–07 override the original concept file.

## Plan discipline
- Execute steps strictly in order; respect Deps; one step at a time; scoped diffs.
- AFTER EVERY COMPLETED STEP, update the active plan docs/07_Plan_V2.md in the same turn:
  tick [x] (or [!] blocked / [~] in progress) → fill "Done: YYYY-MM-DD — summary; files; verification"
  → advance "Current Step" → update the Progress table → add a Decision Log row for any deviation.
- Never tick a step unless its Verify check passed. At phase gates (V2.09, V2.13, V2.18, V2.23, V2.29, V2.36) run `pnpm run ci` and stop for review.

## Conflicts
- Technical precedence: 05_Schema > 04_TRD > 02_AppFlow > 03_UI_Spec > 01_PRD. Scope: 01_PRD wins.
- Hard-to-reverse ambiguity (schema/auth/API/deps) → STOP and ask. Small reversible choices → decide + log.
- Changing a locked decision: get approval → update docs first → log → implement.

## Hard rules
- Never build PRD §6 Non-Goals or R2-reserved tables. Student groups = plans only.
- FREE TIERS ONLY (TRD §13): nothing may need a paid Vercel/Supabase/Resend/Google plan. Uploads go straight to Supabase
  Storage via signed URLs (never through the app server); no long-running server work; no Vercel Cron/Blob/KV;
  no Supabase image transformations.
- Only TRD §2 packages at EXACT versions (pnpm add -E; no ^ or ~). No new deps without a Decision Log entry.
  Forbidden: any ORM, Supabase Auth/@supabase/ssr, NextAuth, Redux/Zustand/Jotai, TanStack Query, UI kits with themes,
  CSS-in-JS, axios, moment, npm `xlsx`, middleware.ts (use src/proxy.ts). pnpm + Node 22 only.
- Browser never calls Supabase directly; the service_role key lives only in `import 'server-only'` modules.
- NEVER send correct_option / explanation / option stats to the client before the attempt is final AND the publish gate
  has passed. Student question reads go only through src/features/attempts/paper.ts → view paper_questions.
- Time + scoring are enforced in SQL (deadline_at + 15 s grace). Client timer is cosmetic.
- PINs/passwords: argon2id + AUTH_PEPPER; never log/store/return plaintext PINs (except the credentials email and the
  one-time manual-PIN dialog); no secrets in the outbox.
- Scope every student query by session.studentId; every admin entry calls requireAdmin().
- New table ⇒ RLS enabled + forced + pgTAP test. Zod at every boundary. Audit rows in the same transaction.
- No dangerouslySetInnerHTML except server-rendered output of src/lib/content/render.ts.
- DB changes: new numbered migration only (never edit one applied to staging/production) → pnpm db:reset && pnpm db:types && pnpm db:test.
  Transactional logic = SQL functions (security definer, search_path pinned, EXECUTE to service_role only).
  src/types/database.ts is generated — never hand-edit.

## Conventions
- Folder structure exactly per TRD §3. Logic in src/features/<domain>/{service,queries,actions}.ts — not in components/routes.
- Server Components by default; 'use client' only for interactive islands.
- Envelope: { ok: true, data } | { ok: false, error: { code, message, field?, meta? } } with canonical ErrorCodes (AppFlow §7.1).
- Use exact route paths, enum values, state names and error codes from the docs.
- Tailwind with design tokens only: no hex literals, no arbitrary values, no inline styles (except dynamic widths).
- All UI strings via the message catalogs (next-intl/server on the server, src/lib/i18n/client.tsx in client components);
  update messages/bn.json AND messages/en.json together. Bangla default. Latin digits.
  Times displayed in Asia/Dhaka.
- Mobile-first (360 px), touch targets ≥ 48 px, one primary action per screen, dark mode via tokens.
- TS strict, no `any`, no non-null assertions on external data. Match surrounding style; comments explain why.
- Before marking done: pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test (+ pnpm db:test if SQL changed,
  + pnpm check:answer-leak if exam/paper code changed).

## Reporting
End each turn with: step ID(s), files changed, verification evidence, new Current Step, Decision Log entries / open questions.
Commit only when asked: one commit per step, message "P<id>: <summary>" (V1) / "V2.<nn>: <summary>" (V2), unless the user specifies one.
